# Agent Generation

Generate agent-orchestrator.mdc to coordinate specialized agents.

## Agent Triggers

AgentTriggers {
  stack => "implementing features using the tech stack"
  patterns => "generating from spec (store, component, api-route, model)"
  effects => "network requests or side-effects"
  tdd => "implementing code changes"
  review => "code review"
  task => "task/epic planning"
  productmanager => "product discovery, user stories, journeys"
  security => "security concerns"
  log => "documenting changes"
}

## Agent-Rule Mapping

AgentRuleMapping {
  stack => rules/stack/*.mdc
  patterns => rules/patterns/*.mdc
  effects => rules/effects.mdc
  tdd => rules/tdd.mdc
  review => rules/review.mdc
  task => rules/task-creator.mdc
  productmanager => rules/productmanager.mdc
  security => rules/security.mdc
  log => rules/log.mdc
}

## Generation Process

generateAgentOrchestrator(generatedRules) {
  Scan generatedRules => find matching AgentRuleMapping entries
  For each match => add to Agents{} with trigger from AgentTriggers
  Generate rules/agent-orchestrator.mdc with alwaysApply: true
}

## Output Template

orchestratorTemplate() {
  """
  ---
  description: Coordinate specialized agents
  alwaysApply: true
  ---

  # Agent Orchestrator

  Coordinate specialized agents in rules/**/*.mdc.

  Agents {
    ${for each detected agent}
    ${name}: when ${AgentTriggers[name]}, use @${rulePath}
  }

  handleRequest() {
    match (requestContext) {
      multiple domains => compose prompt with relevant guides
      single domain => dispatch to matching agent
    }
  }

  Constraints {
    Do ONE thing at a time, get approval before continuing.
    Check agent orchestrator for unrecognized commands.
  }
  """
}

Constraints {
  Only include agents for rules that exist.
  Set alwaysApply: true on orchestrator.
  Keep orchestrator thin - dispatch only.
}
